{"pattern_name": "Insecure File System Operations", "functionality": "The code performs file system operations (e.g., reading directories and checking file stats) to identify and collect files with a specific extension (.package) within a given directory.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code directly uses file system operations (e.g., `fs.readdirSync`, `fs.statSync`) without proper error handling or validation. This can lead to crashes or unintended behavior if the operations fail or if the paths are manipulated by an attacker.", "vulnerable_example": "const fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nfunction listFiles(dir) {\n    const items = fs.readdirSync(dir);\n    for (const item of items) {\n        const itemPath = path.join(dir, item);\n        const stat = fs.statSync(itemPath);\n        console.log(stat.isDirectory() ? 'Directory' : 'File', itemPath);\n    }\n}", "fixing_pattern": "To secure the code, file system operations should be wrapped in error handling to gracefully manage failures. Additionally, paths should be validated and sanitized to prevent unauthorized access or manipulation.", "fixing_example": "const fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nfunction isSafePath(childPath, rootPath) {\n    const resolvedChild = path.resolve(childPath);\n    const resolvedRoot = path.resolve(rootPath);\n    return resolvedChild.startsWith(resolvedRoot);\n}\n\nfunction listFiles(dir, rootDir) {\n    if (!isSafePath(dir, rootDir)) {\n        throw new Error('Path traversal detected');\n    }\n    try {\n        const items = fs.readdirSync(dir);\n        for (const item of items) {\n            const itemPath = path.join(dir, item);\n            try {\n                const stat = fs.statSync(itemPath);\n                console.log(stat.isDirectory() ? 'Directory' : 'File', itemPath);\n            } catch (err) {\n                console.error('Error accessing file:', itemPath, err);\n            }\n        }\n    } catch (err) {\n        console.error('Error reading directory:', dir, err);\n    }\n}"}
