{"pattern_name": "Missing Authorization in Database Operations", "functionality": "The code connects to a SQLite database, creates a table with specified columns and a primary key, and queries the database based on provided conditions. It returns the results of the query.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code lacks proper authorization checks before executing critical database operations, such as creating a table or querying data. This allows unauthorized users to perform potentially harmful actions on the database.", "vulnerable_example": "<?php\nfunction createAndQueryTable($dbname, $table, $columns, $primaryKey, $conditions) {\n    $db = new PDO(\"sqlite:$dbname\");\n    $db->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE, PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION);\n    $columnDefinitions = implode(\", \", $columns);\n    $sql = \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS $table ($columnDefinitions, PRIMARY KEY ($primaryKey))\";\n    $db->exec($sql); // Vulnerable line\n    $query = \"SELECT * FROM $table WHERE $conditions\";\n    $stmt = $db->prepare($query);\n    $stmt->execute();\n    return $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);\n}\n?>", "fixing_pattern": "Implement authorization checks to ensure that only authorized users can perform critical database operations. This can be done by validating user permissions before executing the database query or table creation.", "fixing_example": "<?php\nfunction createAndQueryTable($dbname, $table, $columns, $primaryKey, $conditions, $userRole) {\n    if ($userRole !== 'admin') {\n        throw new Exception(\"Unauthorized access\");\n    }\n    $db = new PDO(\"sqlite:$dbname\");\n    $db->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE, PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION);\n    $columnDefinitions = implode(\", \", $columns);\n    $sql = \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS $table ($columnDefinitions, PRIMARY KEY ($primaryKey))\";\n    $db->exec($sql); // Now protected by authorization check\n    $query = \"SELECT * FROM $table WHERE $conditions\";\n    $stmt = $db->prepare($query);\n    $stmt->execute();\n    return $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);\n}\n?>"}
{"pattern_name": "Missing CSRF Protection in HTTP POST Handler", "functionality": "The code handles user registration by accepting a POST request with user registration data, validating the input, checking for existing users, and adding a new user to the repository.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The HTTP POST handler lacks the `[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]` attribute, making it vulnerable to Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attacks. Without this attribute, the application cannot verify that the request originated from an authenticated user, allowing malicious actors to forge requests and perform unauthorized actions.", "vulnerable_example": "[HttpPost]\npublic IActionResult UpdateProfile([FromBody] UserProfileModel profile)\n{\n    if (profile == null)\n    {\n        return BadRequest(\"Invalid profile data.\");\n    }\n\n    userRepository.UpdateProfile(profile);\n    return Ok(\"Profile updated successfully.\");\n}", "fixing_pattern": "To mitigate CSRF vulnerabilities, the `[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]` attribute should be added to the HTTP POST handler. This ensures that the request includes a valid anti-forgery token, verifying its authenticity and preventing unauthorized requests.", "fixing_example": "[HttpPost]\n[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]\npublic IActionResult RegisterUser([FromBody] UserRegistrationModel userRegistration)\n{\n    if (userRegistration == null)\n    {\n        return BadRequest(\"Invalid user registration data.\");\n    }\n\n    if (!ModelState.IsValid)\n    {\n        return BadRequest(ModelState);\n    }\n\n    if (userRepository.UserExists(userRegistration.Username))\n    {\n        return BadRequest(\"Username already exists.\");\n    }\n\n    if (!userRepository.IsEmailValid(userRegistration.Email))\n    {\n        return BadRequest(\"Invalid email address.\");\n    }\n\n    var user = new User\n    {\n        Username = userRegistration.Username,\n        Email = userRegistration.Email,\n        PasswordHash = HashPassword(userRegistration.Password)\n    };\n\n    userRepository.AddUser(user);\n    return Ok(\"User registered successfully.\");\n}"}
{"pattern_name": "Unsafe Exception Handling in Token Generation", "functionality": "The code generates a JWT token for a user with an expiration time and logs the user's successful login.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Catching a generic Exception and logging the error message without proper handling, then rethrowing a custom exception.", "vulnerable_example": "try {\n  instance.add(Calendar.HOUR, 24);\n  String token =\n      JWT.create()\n          .withClaim(\"userId\", user.getId())\n          .withClaim(\"name\", user.getName())\n          .withExpiresAt(instance.getTime())\n          .sign(Algorithm.HMAC256(\"IOTDB:\" + InetAddress.getLocalHost().getHostAddress()));\n  logger.info(user.getName() + \"login successfully\");\n  return token;\n} catch (Exception e) {\n  logger.info(e.getMessage());\n  throw new BaseException(ErrorCode.GET_TOKEN_FAIL, ErrorCode.GET_TOKEN_FAIL_MSG);\n}", "fixing_pattern": "The code was completely replaced with a simple HTML response for a welcome page, removing the token generation logic entirely.", "fixing_example": "@GetMapping(\"/\")\npublic String welcome() {\n  String str =\n      \"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n\"\n          + \"<html lang=\\\"ch\\\">\\n\"\n          + \"<head>\\n\"\n          + \"    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n\"\n          + \"    <title>welcome</title>\\n\"\n          + \"</head>\\n\"\n          + \"<body>\\n\"\n          + \"<h1>You have successfully started IoTDB-Workbench backend application!</h1>\\n\"\n          + \"<h2>For a better experience with IOTDB-Workbench, Please refer to the <a href=\\\"https://github.com/loveher147/iotdb-admin/blob/main/backend/doc/deploy.md\\\">deployment documentation</a> for deployment</h2>\\n\"\n          + \"</body>\\n\"\n          + \"</html>\";\n  return str;\n}"}
{"pattern_name": "Global Credential Exposure in Middleware", "functionality": "The code uses global middleware to set authentication credentials for all requests, including those not intended for the target service.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Using global middleware (e.g., `HttpAuthMiddleware`) to set authentication credentials for all requests, which can expose credentials to unintended targets.", "vulnerable_example": "Using `http_user` and `http_pass` spider attributes to set credentials globally for all requests, including non-Splash requests like `robots.txt`.", "fixing_pattern": "Replace global credential settings with per-request credential configuration or use service-specific settings to ensure credentials are only sent to the intended target.", "fixing_example": "Using `SPLASH_USER` and `SPLASH_PASS` settings or setting credentials via the `splash_headers` parameter on a per-request basis."}
