{"pattern_name": "Unvalidated Server Information", "functionality": "The code processes server information such as hostname, port, and prefix for establishing connections.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Lack of validation for server information before using it to establish connections.", "vulnerable_example": "cfg.set(\"server\", \"hostname\", self.server_hostname)", "fixing_pattern": "Adding validation checks for server information to ensure it is safe and correct before use.", "fixing_example": "conf[\"server\"][\"hostname\"] = self.server_hostname"}
{"pattern_name": "Insufficient Error Handling and Information Exposure", "functionality": "The code formats error messages and includes detailed exception information in the response, which is exposed to the client.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code unconditionally includes detailed exception information (such as stack traces) in the response without checking if the error type is allowed or if the application is in debug mode.", "vulnerable_example": "if settings.DEBUG:\n    lines = []\n    if isinstance(exc, BaseException):\n        for line in traceback.format_exception(type(exc), exc, exc.__traceback__):\n            lines.extend(line.rstrip().splitlines())\n    result['extensions']['exception']['stacktrace'] = lines", "fixing_pattern": "The fix adds a check to ensure that detailed error information is only included if the error type is allowed or if the application is in debug mode. Additionally, it replaces the error message with a generic one for unauthorized error types.", "fixing_example": "if type(exc) not in ALLOWED_ERRORS and not settings.DEBUG:\n    result['message'] = INTERNAL_ERROR_MESSAGE\nif settings.DEBUG:\n    lines = []\n    if isinstance(exc, BaseException):\n        for line in traceback.format_exception(type(exc), exc, exc.__traceback__):\n            lines.extend(line.rstrip().splitlines())\n    result['extensions']['exception']['stacktrace'] = lines"}
