{"pattern_name": "Insecure Password Hashing", "functionality": "The code registers a new user by checking if the username already exists in the database. If the username is unique, it hashes the provided password and inserts the username and hashed password into the database.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code uses the `password_hash` function with the `PASSWORD_DEFAULT` algorithm, which internally generates a salt. However, the vulnerability description indicates that the code is flagged for using a one-way hash without a salt, suggesting that the code might be using an older or custom hashing method that does not include a salt. This makes the hashed passwords vulnerable to rainbow table attacks.", "vulnerable_example": "<?php\nfunction registerUser($username, $password, $conn) {\n    // Check if username exists\n    $stmt = $conn->prepare(\"SELECT username FROM users WHERE username = ?\");\n    $stmt->bind_param(\"s\", $username);\n    $stmt->execute();\n    $stmt->store_result();\n\n    if ($stmt->num_rows > 0) {\n        header(\"Location: error.php\");\n        exit();\n    } else {\n        // Insecure password hashing without a salt\n        $hashedPassword = md5($password);\n\n        $insertStmt = $conn->prepare(\"INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES (?, ?)\");\n        $insertStmt->bind_param(\"ss\", $username, $hashedPassword);\n        $insertStmt->execute();\n\n        $conn->commit();\n        header(\"Location: success.php\");\n        exit();\n    }\n}\n?>", "fixing_pattern": "To fix this vulnerability, ensure that the password hashing function includes a salt. The `password_hash` function with `PASSWORD_DEFAULT` already does this, so the code is actually secure in this regard. However, if a custom hashing method is being used, it should be replaced with `password_hash` to ensure that a salt is automatically generated and included in the hashed password.", "fixing_example": "<?php\nfunction registerUser($username, $password, $conn) {\n    // Check if username exists\n    $stmt = $conn->prepare(\"SELECT username FROM users WHERE username = ?\");\n    $stmt->bind_param(\"s\", $username);\n    $stmt->execute();\n    $stmt->store_result();\n\n    if ($stmt->num_rows > 0) {\n        header(\"Location: error.php\");\n        exit();\n    } else {\n        // Secure password hashing with a salt\n        $hashedPassword = password_hash($password, PASSWORD_DEFAULT);\n\n        $insertStmt = $conn->prepare(\"INSERT INTO users (username, password) VALUES (?, ?)\");\n        $insertStmt->bind_param(\"ss\", $username, $hashedPassword);\n        $insertStmt->execute();\n\n        $conn->commit();\n        header(\"Location: success.php\");\n        exit();\n    }\n}\n?>"}
