{"pattern_name": "Insecure Path Resolution in Recursive Directory Traversal", "functionality": "The code recursively traverses directories to find files matching a specified name, using dynamically constructed paths.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code recursively constructs and resolves paths without ensuring they remain within the intended directory. This can lead to path traversal attacks if an attacker manipulates the input to access unauthorized files or directories.", "vulnerable_example": "const fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nfunction traverseDirectory(dirPath) {\n    const files = fs.readdirSync(dirPath);\n    for (const file of files) {\n        const filePath = path.join(dirPath, file);\n        const stats = fs.lstatSync(filePath);\n        if (stats.isDirectory()) {\n            traverseDirectory(filePath);\n        }\n    }\n}", "fixing_pattern": "Ensure all resolved paths remain within the intended directory by validating the resolved path against a safe base path. Use absolute paths and restrict traversal to predefined safe directories.", "fixing_example": "const fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nfunction traverseDirectory(basePath, dirPath) {\n    const resolvedPath = path.resolve(basePath, dirPath);\n    if (!resolvedPath.startsWith(basePath)) {\n        throw new Error('Invalid directory path');\n    }\n    const files = fs.readdirSync(resolvedPath);\n    for (const file of files) {\n        const filePath = path.join(resolvedPath, file);\n        const stats = fs.lstatSync(filePath);\n        if (stats.isDirectory()) {\n            traverseDirectory(basePath, filePath);\n        }\n    }\n}"}
