{"pattern_name": "Unsafe Content-Type Handling in File Uploads", "functionality": "The system processes uploaded files and serves them with a Content-Type header that can be manipulated by users.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The system accepts and serves files with arbitrary Content-Type headers without proper validation or sanitization, potentially allowing malicious content to be executed in the context of the application.", "vulnerable_example": "def serve_file(file):\n    content_type = file.content_type\n    response = HttpResponse(file.content, content_type=content_type)\n    response['Content-Disposition'] = 'inline'\n    return response", "fixing_pattern": "Implement strict Content-Type validation and enforce safe Content-Disposition headers for uploaded files. Additionally, implement Content-Security-Policy headers to mitigate potential script execution.", "fixing_example": "def serve_file(file):\n    allowed_types = ['image/jpeg', 'image/png']\n    if file.content_type not in allowed_types:\n        raise ValueError('Unsupported file type')\n    response = HttpResponse(file.content, content_type=file.content_type)\n    response['Content-Disposition'] = 'attachment; filename=\"%s\"' % file.name\n    response['Content-Security-Policy'] = \"default-src 'self'\"\n    return response"}
