{"pattern_name": "SQL Injection via String Concatenation", "functionality": "The code performs CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations on a SQLite database by dynamically constructing SQL queries based on user-provided inputs.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The vulnerability arises from directly concatenating user-provided inputs (such as table names, conditions, and data) into SQL query strings. This allows an attacker to inject malicious SQL code, leading to unauthorized database access or manipulation.", "vulnerable_example": "query = f\"SELECT * FROM {table} WHERE {condition}\"\ncursor.execute(query)", "fixing_pattern": "To prevent SQL injection, use parameterized queries or prepared statements. This ensures that user inputs are treated as data rather than executable code. Additionally, validate and sanitize inputs to ensure they conform to expected formats.", "fixing_example": "query = \"SELECT * FROM ? WHERE ?\"\ncursor.execute(query, (table, condition))"}
{"pattern_name": "Misconfigured Protocol Upgrade Handling", "functionality": "The code is responsible for configuring protocol upgrade settings, specifically handling the transition from HTTP/1.1 to HTTP/2.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The vulnerable code directly modifies a configuration structure (cfg->modern_tls_only) without proper validation or synchronization, which can lead to misconfiguration when multiple requests attempt to upgrade the protocol simultaneously.", "vulnerable_example": "static const char *h2_conf_set_modern_tls_only(cmd_parms *parms, void *arg, const char *value)\n{\n    h2_config *cfg = (h2_config *)h2_config_sget(parms->server);\n    if (!strcasecmp(value, \"On\")) {\n        cfg->modern_tls_only = 1;\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    else if (!strcasecmp(value, \"Off\")) {\n        cfg->modern_tls_only = 0;\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    (void)arg;\n    return \"value must be On or Off\";\n}", "fixing_pattern": "The fix introduces a safer configuration mechanism by using a macro (CONFIG_CMD_SET) to set the configuration value, ensuring proper synchronization and validation during the protocol upgrade process.", "fixing_example": "static const char *h2_conf_set_push(cmd_parms *cmd, void *dirconf, const char *value)\n{\n    if (!strcasecmp(value, \"On\")) {\n        CONFIG_CMD_SET(cmd, dirconf, H2_CONF_PUSH, 1);\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    else if (!strcasecmp(value, \"Off\")) {\n        CONFIG_CMD_SET(cmd, dirconf, H2_CONF_PUSH, 0);\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    return \"value must be On or Off\";\n}"}
