{"pattern_name": "Unsanitized JSON Error Message Handling", "functionality": "The code processes JSON data and generates error messages that are displayed to users without proper sanitization.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The vulnerability arises when JSON error messages are directly incorporated into web responses without proper escaping or sanitization, allowing potential injection of malicious scripts.", "vulnerable_example": "The specific vulnerable code is not shown in the commit, but the pattern would involve something like:\n\n```python\nerror_message = json.loads(request.data)['error']\nreturn f'<div>{error_message}</div>'\n```", "fixing_pattern": "The fix involves ensuring that any user-controlled input that is included in web responses is properly escaped or sanitized to prevent XSS attacks.", "fixing_example": "The fix would involve using proper escaping mechanisms, such as:\n\n```python\nfrom markupsafe import escape\n\nerror_message = json.loads(request.data)['error']\nreturn f'<div>{escape(error_message)}</div>'\n```"}
{"pattern_name": "Missing CSRF Token Validation", "functionality": "The application processes sensitive actions via POST requests without verifying the presence of a CSRF token.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Accepting and processing sensitive requests without CSRF token validation, making it possible for attackers to forge requests from a user's browser.", "vulnerable_example": "// Vulnerable code accepting POST requests without CSRF token validation\n@POST\n@Path(\"/execute\")\npublic Response executeAction(@FormParam(\"action\") String action) {\n    // Execute the action without CSRF token validation\n    execute(action);\n    return Response.ok().build();\n}", "fixing_pattern": "Adding CSRF token validation to ensure that requests originate from the application's own forms and not from malicious sites.", "fixing_example": "// Fixed code with CSRF token validation\n@POST\n@Path(\"/execute\")\npublic Response executeAction(@FormParam(\"action\") String action, @HeaderParam(\"X-CSRF-Token\") String csrfToken) {\n    if (!validateCsrfToken(csrfToken)) {\n        return Response.status(Response.Status.FORBIDDEN).build();\n    }\n    execute(action);\n    return Response.ok().build();\n}"}
{"pattern_name": "Missing CSRF Protection in HTTP POST Handler", "functionality": "The code handles HTTP POST requests to create a new instance of a view model, populates it with data from the request, validates the data, and returns the populated view model as a response.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code does not include the `[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]` attribute on the HTTP POST handler, making it vulnerable to Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attacks. CSRF allows an attacker to trick a user into performing unintended actions on a web application in which they are authenticated.", "vulnerable_example": "[HttpPost]\npublic IActionResult UpdateUserProfile()\n{\n    var userProfile = new UserProfile();\n    userProfile.Email = HttpContext.Request.Form[\"email\"];\n    userProfile.Password = HttpContext.Request.Form[\"password\"];\n    return Ok(userProfile);\n}", "fixing_pattern": "To mitigate CSRF vulnerabilities, the `[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]` attribute should be added to the HTTP POST handler. This ensures that the request includes a valid anti-forgery token, which is verified by the server to confirm the request's authenticity.", "fixing_example": "[HttpPost]\n[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]\npublic IActionResult CreateTriggersDetail()\n{\n    if (HttpContext.Request.Method != \"POST\")\n    {\n        return BadRequest(\"Only POST requests are allowed.\");\n    }\n    var triggersDetailViewModel = new TriggersDetailViewModel();\n    try\n    {\n        triggersDetailViewModel.Name = HttpContext.Request.Form[\"name\"];\n        triggersDetailViewModel.Value = HttpContext.Request.Form[\"value\"];\n        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(triggersDetailViewModel.Name) || string.IsNullOrEmpty(triggersDetailViewModel.Value))\n        {\n            return BadRequest(\"Name and Value are required fields.\");\n        }\n        return Ok(triggersDetailViewModel);\n    }\n    catch (Exception ex)\n    {\n        return StatusCode(500, \"An error occurred while processing your request.\");\n    }\n}"}
