{"pattern_name": "SQL Injection via String Concatenation", "functionality": "The code retrieves a user from the database by constructing a SQL query dynamically using string concatenation with user-provided input.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Using string concatenation to construct SQL queries with user-provided input, which allows malicious input to alter the query structure.", "vulnerable_example": "Statement getuserStatement = connection.createStatement();\nResultSet resultUser = getuserStatement.executeQuery(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE user_id = '\" + userId + \"'\");", "fixing_pattern": "Using prepared statements with parameterized queries to separate SQL logic from user input, preventing malicious input from altering the query structure.", "fixing_example": "PreparedStatement p = connection.prepareStatement(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE user_id = ?\");\np.setInt(1, userId);\nResultSet resultUser = p.executeQuery();"}
