{"pattern_name": "Exposure of Sensitive Information in Configuration", "functionality": "The code handles sensitive information (e.g., passwords) in a configuration object and exposes it directly in the configuration.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code directly assigns and retrieves sensitive information (e.g., passwords) in the configuration object without proper masking or encryption.", "vulnerable_example": "TfsMaterial material = new TfsMaterial(new GoCipher(), new UrlArgument(\"http://url/\"), \"user\", \"domain\", \"password\", \"$project/path/\");\nTfsMaterialConfig config = (TfsMaterialConfig) material.config();\nassertThat(config.getPassword()).isEqualTo(\"password\");\nassertThat(config.getEncryptedPassword()).isNotNull();", "fixing_pattern": "The code now ensures that sensitive information (e.g., passwords) is not exposed in the configuration object by masking or removing it when retrieving attributes.", "fixing_example": "TfsMaterial material = new TfsMaterial(new UrlArgument(\"http://username:password@tfsrepo.com\"), \"username\", \"domain\", \"password\", \"$project/path/\");\nMap<String, Object> attributes = material.getAttributes(false);\nassertThat(attributes.get(\"type\")).isEqualTo(\"tfs\");\nMap<String, Object> configuration = (Map<String, Object>) attributes.get(\"tfs-configuration\");\nassertThat(configuration.get(\"url\")).isEqualTo(\"http://username:******@tfsrepo.com\");\nassertThat(configuration.get(\"domain\")).isEqualTo(\"domain\");\nassertThat(configuration.get(\"username\")).isEqualTo(\"username\");\nassertThat(configuration.get(\"password\")).isNull();\nassertThat(configuration.get(\"project-path\")).isEqualTo(\"$project/path/\");"}
{"pattern_name": "Incomplete Error Status Assignment", "functionality": "The code processes a request and handles errors by returning error codes, but doesn't always set the status message before returning.", "vulnerable_pattern": "Returning an error code without setting the status message, which can lead to incomplete error reporting and debugging difficulties.", "vulnerable_example": "if (code)\n    return code;", "fixing_pattern": "Ensuring that all error return paths set the appropriate status message before returning.", "fixing_example": "if (code) {\n    *status = \"DECODE_PA_FOR_USER\";\n    return code;\n}"}
